            <ArticleTitle>Joint pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>247-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article reviews the approach an internist might take with a patient with joint pain. It emphasizes aspects of the history and physical examination that help yield a diagnosis. The use of simple laboratory tests is reviewed, and common questions are answered. Some general management issues are discussed, although disease-specific therapy is beyond the scope of this article. It is hoped that this article will help an internist successfully diagnose most patients who present with joint pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
